# Default flags for `act` (nektos/act). Applied to every invocation.
#
# Pin the runner image so `act` works out of the box: without this it prompts
# for an image size on first run, and its slim default cannot build this
# workspace at all.
#
# `full-latest` rather than the 540 MB `act-latest` / `runner-latest` because
# the bindgen-backed `-sys` crates (libzwo-sys, libqhyccd-sys, libsvbony-sys)
# need **libclang** in the container. Neither slim image carries it, so
# `act -W .github/workflows/test.yml -j required` dies in ~16 s inside
# libzwo-sys's build script with "Unable to find libclang". The
# `*_SKIP_NATIVE_LINK` vars those workflows set do not help — they skip the
# native *link*, not the binding generation, which is unconditional.
#
# The cost is real and worth knowing before the first run: ~18 GB compressed
# (measured on the amd64 manifest, 2026-08-30), and more on disk. It is pulled
# once and cached. If that trade stops being worth it, the alternative is to
# have the workflows install libclang themselves and drop back to
# `catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest` here.
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:full-latest
